<description>
Convert each hollow 3x3 symbol to one pixel and slide the pixels clockwise from the marked edge.

Input structure
- The grid has a background, one full-edge marker line, and monochrome hollow 3x3 foreground symbols.
- The symbols lie on a coarse row/column lattice; fully empty lattice rows or columns are absent from the output.

Rule
- Replace each hollow 3x3 symbol with one pixel of its color in the corresponding coarse-grid cell.
- The marker edge gives the compaction direction by clockwise border travel: top -> right, right -> down, bottom -> left, left -> up.
- Preserve the order of non-background pixels while sliding them as far as possible in that direction.

Key insight
- The large picture is a scaled symbolic grid, and the blue edge marker acts as a gravity direction rather than as output content.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "hollow 3x3 foreground symbols collapsed to one coarse-grid pixel each; the full-edge blue marker selects the path direction",
  "path": "straight along each coarse row or column in clockwise border direction from the marker edge: top->right, right->down, bottom->left, left->up; stop when packed against the boundary or previous pixel",
  "trajectory": "stably compact all non-background coarse pixels in each parallel line, preserving their order",
  "transform": "discard the blue marker and fully empty coarse rows or columns; replace each hollow 3x3 symbol by its color",
  "grid_shape": "occupied coarse lattice after empty rows or columns are dropped"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 30x30, background 0
  marker:
    color: 1 [observed]
    position: one full edge row or col (top/right/bottom/left)
    compaction_map: top->right, right->down, bottom->left, left->up
  symbols:
    shape: hollow 3x3 ring (8 pixels, center is bg)
    lattice_spacing: 4 in both dims, with one gap of 8 in the 6-cell dim
    lattice_dims: 7 cells parallel to marker edge x 6 cells perpendicular (split 3+gap+3)
  color_regions:
    dominant: color 8 [observed fixed]; spans all 7 positions in one dim, 3 in the other (on compaction-target side); fill 13-17 of 21
    color_A: non-bg color other than 1 or 8; 3x3 block (rows 0-2 of 7-dim, opposite half from dominant); fill 6-8 of 9
    color_B: non-bg color other than 1 or 8 and distinct from color_A; 3x3 block (rows 4-6 of 7-dim, opposite half from dominant); fill 6-8 of 9
    separator: row/col index 3 in the 7-dim is always empty in the multi-color half [observed]
  output: symbolic grid (7x6 or 6x7) with non-bg pixels compacted in compaction direction, preserving order per row/col

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick marker side (top/right/bottom/left) and derive compaction direction.
    2. Build symbolic grid (7x6 or 6x7 depending on side).
       - Use fixed dominant color 8; choose two distinct accent colors not in {0,1,8}.
       - Fill dominant region (3x7 or 7x3) with 13-17 cells randomly.
       - Fill color_A region (3x3) with 6-8 cells randomly.
       - Fill color_B region (3x3) with 6-8 cells randomly.
       - Ensure row/col 3 in the multi-color half is all-bg.
    3. Compact the symbolic grid to produce expected output (verify non-trivial).
    4. Expand symbolic grid to 30x30 physical grid by placing hollow 3x3 at each filled lattice cell, with spacing 4 (and 8 at the big gap), offset from marker edge by 2 and from other edges by 1.
    5. Place marker (full edge row/col of color 1) on the chosen side.
```
</generation_spec>
